v2.0.13 Kohly Edition - Candidate release

New: In new_product.zul and new_acquirable_material.zul, now is possible to scan a bar code and if the product is included in
	open4goods-data-open database, or in https://go-upc.com/, the name field is filled out automatically. An Internet connection
	is required for go-upc.

Fix: With RAW printing mode, after collecting an order, the ticket encoded in the URL wasn't printed. Solved not using
	that URL field to get the content to print

Fix: In public class ProduceButtonComposer, back to the previous approach of printing three feed lines at the end of the 
	production allocation ticket. This is because in RAW printing (no CUPS) computer's printer settings aren't available 
	to control that, and RAW is the most popular printing method. An improvement could be to add a setting to printer 
	profile configuration controlling such behaviour.
		
